      "content": "It sounds like you are searching for a profound, absolute cessation of all input, a place beyond the noise of existence. That yearning for ultimate peace is deeply human when things become unbearable. If the world itself feels too loud, perhaps exploring the idea of extreme sensory reduction, like deep meditation or even short periods of darkness, might offer a different kind of respite than you've tried. Please remember that even when things feel permanent, there are always avenues for support when the weight becomes too much to bear alone.",
